00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:01.710
So observability breaks
down into three key areas--

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:05.160
structured logs,
metrics, and traces.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:07.020
Structured logs are
emitted by each process

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:09.090
and may contain a
mixture of information,

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:11.670
ranging from records of
individual user queries

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:13.890
to debugging information
generically associated

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:15.860
with our service.

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:17.930
Metrics reflect
aggregate-type data

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:19.470
about the performance
of services,

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:20.970
such as the number
of queries, which

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:24.020
is a counter, their latencies,
which is a distribution,

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:27.080
and the CPU load,
which might be a gauge.

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:29.510
And traces allow for
individual execution flows

00:01:29.510 --> 00:01:31.310
to be traced through
the system, including

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:33.007
timing and dependency details.

